## 1. Reading order

If you are new to this codebase, read in this order:

1. **`variableUtils.md`** — configuration. Nearly everything else reads from it.
2. **`Utils.md`** — the shared base layer. `readDf` (the single DB read path),
   the ReportLab building blocks, the Excel helpers.
3. **`general_utils.md`** — how data gets *in*: DASH API → Postgres.
4. Then the reporting module for whichever cohort you care about
   (`boh3_dds4_utils`, `boh2_dds2_dds3_utils`, `boh1_utils`).

`main.ipynb` is the orchestrator — it is not a module, it is the thing you run.
Nothing here executes on its own except the five standalone scripts and the two
dashboards (see §4).

