**Reading the diagram.** Thirteen import edges exist between these modules: six
point at `Utils`, six at `variableUtils`, one at `gradio_utils`. Every one of them
is an edge into the config or shared-core layer — **no reporting module imports
another reporting module**, and only the `Utils` edges carry actual function calls
(the `variableUtils`/`gradio_utils` edges are constants only).

Everything else is coupled through the **database**, not through imports:
`general_utils` writes the tables and each reporting module queries them
independently. That is why most modules can be changed in isolation — and also why
a schema change in `rawform_forms_v3` breaks several files at once with no import
graph to warn you.

