### 6.5 Silent-wrong-answer risks

These produce output that looks fine and is not:

- **`risk_report._buildAnalytics` joins three sheets positionally via `.values`,
  with no key.** Any row-order difference silently misattributes every rating and
  practice-readiness figure to the wrong student.
- **`boh2_dds2_dds3_utils.getFlaggedFormDetails` reads `assessor_data->'scales'`
  directly** instead of the student-fallback accessor, so BOH1/BOH2 and all Smile
  Squad forms can never be flagged.
- **`boh3_dds4_utils.addPbnLeaveColumns` catches bare `Exception` and fills 0s**,
  making a missing input workbook indistinguishable from a clean cohort.
- **`build_canned_comments` caches embeddings keyed only on register name**; if
  the input changes, `zip(texts, labels)` truncates to the shorter list with no
  error.
- **`flagging_utils`: NaN never flags**, so single-form and missing-data students
  read as clean; and `high_es_lvl2` can never fire at its default threshold.
- ~~**`flagging_utils` matched `role` and `patient_details` by LABEL only**~~ —
  FIXED 2026-08-18. `role_counts.get("Operator")` / `pd_counts.get("I saw a
  patient")` never matched the v3 CODE spelling (`O`, `ISP`), so on a code-shaped
  pull `operator_count`, `pct_operator` and `patient_seen` were **zero** and
  `low_pt_seen` fired on the wrong students. `normalizeRole` /
  `normalizePatientDetail` now fold both spellings.
- ~~**`general_utils` built `clinical_incident` from the multi-select shape only**~~
  — FIXED 2026-08-18 in the loader *and* at read time
  (`boh2_dds2_dds3_utils.clinicalIncidentSqlExpr`). The 2026 form templates use a
  radio plus a text field, so the column was NULL and **every** incident report —
  flagging and cohort — showed zero. 159 incidents were invisible. Rows already in
  `rawform_forms_v3` keep the NULL until a reload; the read-time path covers them.
- **Two "score" numbers now coexist and legitimately differ** (2026-08-18).
  `flagging_utils` Summary `Score` is form-weighted; the Section Score Pivot's
  section cells and `Overall (per item)` are item-weighted. On DDS2 FHY the gap
  reached 0.064 and moved one student 43 rank places. `FlaggingConfig.scoreWeighting`
  chooses which one `avg_score` and `low_score` use; slopes stay per form.
- **`general_utils`: all DDS2 date filters use `datetimeutc::date`**, correct only
  while the Postgres session timezone is `Australia/Melbourne`. Nothing sets or
  asserts it.
- **Both Gradio dashboards mix naive and tz-aware datetimes** in date filtering —
  off by 10–11 hours on a UTC host.
- **`boh1_utils` does not handle student-only checklists** although `Config.xlsx`
  records that BOH1 has them; the SQL hard-codes `submitted_by_assessor = true`,
  so those items vanish silently.

