## 8. How this documentation was produced

Every function signature, line number, constant value and call edge in these docs
was extracted from the source with Python's `ast` module, not read off by eye. The
call graph resolves a call to `f()` inside module *M* by checking, in order: a
top-level `def f` in *M*; an explicit `from X import f`; then transitively
star-imported modules. Attribute calls (`pd.read_sql`, `df.groupby`) into
third-party libraries are excluded — 671 edges are within this codebase.

Behaviour descriptions, gotchas and the "silent wrong answer" analysis come from
reading the source. Where a doc states that something is broken, it cites the
line.

**Keeping it current.** The extraction has not been re-run since 2026-08-14, so
line numbers and prose describe that snapshot. Later sessions amend the affected
module doc in place with a **dated** note rather than silently editing the
generated text, so it stays obvious which parts are original and which are
patches. Amended so far: `flagging_utils.md` (§0 and §7),
`boh2_dds2_dds3_utils.md` (`clinicalIncidentSqlExpr`, `getDataDf`,
`getCriticalIncidentDf`), `general_utils.md` (`getInsertSqlRawform_forms_v3`
item 6) — all 2026-08-18, see
`_handover_docs/HANDOVER_dds2_clinic_flagging_fhy.md`; and `boh3_dds4_utils.md`
(§0 — weakness analytics, all-comments, PDF cover/contents & page numbers) on
2026-09-16, see `_handover_docs/HANDOVER_student_report_weakness_comments_and_toc.md`.
A full regeneration would
replace all of them; §2 of `python-reference-docs` in project memory has the
recipe.

**Known limits.** Dynamic dispatch (`getattr`, dict-of-functions, registry
lookups such as `flagging_utils.SHEET_REGISTRY`) is invisible to static analysis,
so a few real call relationships are missing from the graph — the registry-driven
sheet builders in `flagging_utils` and `boh3_dds4_utils` are the main case, and
they are documented by hand in those modules' docs. `main.ipynb`'s own calls were
found by parsing the notebook's `import` statements first and then name-matching
**only within modules the notebook actually imports** — so notebook-local helpers
sharing a module function's name (`main`, `getBannerDrawer`, `_hdr`) no longer
register as entry points. The individual docs for `generate_reports`,
`generate_mcex_reports`, `build_canned_comments` and `risk_report` note these
collisions explicitly.
